<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Undi</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1880 CE (approx.) · capital Mano</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western Chewa kingdom of the Undi, an offshoot of Maravi whose lands held gold mines worked by Portuguese traders.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Undi dynasty was founded in the 17th century by a member of the Phiri ruling clan of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-maravi">Kingdom of Maravi</a> who, according to tradition, quarrelled with the Kalonga and led followers west. He established his capital at Mano near the Kapoche river, on the borderlands of present-day <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-mozambique">Mozambique</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Undi ruled through kin and territorial chiefs who sent tribute and recognised his ritual primacy, including over rain shrines. The kingdom traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and cloth with the Portuguese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tete">Tete</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zumbo">Zumbo</a>, and in the 18th century Portuguese and Goan miners worked gold deposits in Undi territory under licence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chewa">Chewa</a> culture, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyau">Nyau</a> masked societies, flourished.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Decline set in during the 19th century as Afro-Portuguese warlords and, from the 1830s, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngoni">Ngoni</a> invaders raided its lands. By around 1880 central authority had collapsed. The Undi title survives as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chewa">Chewa</a> paramount chieftaincy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1650 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:4.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mano</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Chewa religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chichewa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/zambia">Zambia</a>, <a href="/countries/mozambique">Mozambique</a>, <a href="/countries/malawi">Malawi</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Undi, Chewa kingdom of Undi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1765&amp;focus=kingdom-of-undi" aria-label="Kingdom of Undi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5408 2731 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Undi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5956 2992h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5728 2987h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5728 2987h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Zambia. <a href="/atlas?year=1765&amp;focus=kingdom-of-undi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
